| PR-J — completion audit/freeze | Implemented and closed | `npm run phase15:audit` returns `complete-frozen`; localReady, publicationReady, and externalReady are all true |

## Publication readiness boundary

`localReady` reports normal repository validation. `publicationReady` is produced only by `npm run ci:prepublish` for the exact candidate. Per ADR-0018, prepublication evidence is bound to the candidate's git tree content hash rather than its commit SHA, because a real GitHub merge always server-generates a new commit SHA even when file content is unchanged; a tree-content change still invalidates prepublication evidence, but a merge-generated commit-identity change alone does not. `externalReady` requires real external evidence. Provider handoff preserves compact gate/evidence state without transferring transcripts.

The publication manifest supplies the required PR title/body structure. One policy validates local files, GitHub pull-request events, and the title/body read back after GitHub creation or update. GitHub remains an independent verifier and cannot be replaced by model confidence.

## Simulated orchestration boundary

The orchestration module remains a simulation for the business broker. The engineering-agent platform now has credential-gated HTTP adapters and a read-only ephemeral Codex CLI transport for controlled evals, but no persistent worker or autonomous production executor. Provider transports have no deployment authority.

## Execution-budget conformance correction

The bounded frozen-contract correction authorized by approved ADR-0023 is implemented at the controlled provider boundary. An immutable `ExecutionBudgetLineage` and metadata-only `ExecutionBudgetLedger` now own cumulative `maxModelCalls` and `maxOutputTokens` enforcement across requests, retries, model re-entry, provider transitions, and failure paths. Atomic reservations are written to the existing append-only local/CI evidence boundary before direct provider invocation; uncertain invocation is charged conservatively, while authoritative terminal usage releases only unused token capacity.

The exact Claude Messages HTTP and OpenAI Responses HTTP paths are conformant because each performs one visible request with no hidden transport retry, receives a hard admitted `max_tokens` or reasoning-inclusive `max_output_tokens` cap, and settles from authoritative usage. Codex CLI remains noncompliant and now fails with a non-retryable policy error before subprocess execution. This correction adds no provider, routing behavior, role-budget change, gateway, harness registration, deployment, or release authority; OpenCode/Groq execution remains outside this runtime and fail-closed.

## Authorized Phase 1.5 scope

- machine-readable role contracts and deterministic agent CI;
- automatic metadata-only run, token, context, cache, latency, retry, routing, and quality telemetry;
- bounded context selection and canonical provider-neutral prompt compilation;
- explainable provider-routing benchmarks and failure/capacity handoff;
- deterministic pre-tool allow, ask, or deny policy;
- functional, security, handoff, failure, and regression eval fixtures;
- correlated agent, quality, artifact, deployment, verification, approval, and rollback evidence.

Provider-native caching may be used and measured. Embeddings, vector storage, full RAG, graph indexing, semantic caching, and learned routing remain reserved extension points, not Phase 1.5 implementation work.

## Completion boundary

Phase 1.5 completes only when every gate in ADR-0017 and the completion audit has executable evidence. Current status is **complete-frozen**, verified live via `npm run phase15:audit` (see the [Phase 1.5 completion audit](/docs/plans/phase-1-5-completion-audit/) for the literal command output, evidence, and re-verification instructions). Per that page's own freeze rule and this project's freshness discipline, re-run the command before trusting this status in a later session rather than treating it as durable. Phase 1.6 planning has begun under the [Phase 1.6 master spec](/docs/plans/phase-1-6-master-spec/); frozen Phase 1.5 remains the execution constitution that Phase 1.6 work executes through.

The supplied Tier 1 sources still define a broader brokered company with durable business work units, isolated execution, provider invocation, persistent audit, majority convergence, and human approvals. Those capabilities remain target state unless a current page, implementation, and test prove otherwise.
